cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Voice Scribe: a local-first real-time speech-to-text capture primitive"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it along with the works it
  implements — particularly Radford et al. (Whisper) and Liu et al.
  (the local agreement policy). See docs/references.md.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yanez
    given-names: Johnraymond
    alias: JohnYanez95
repository-code: "https://github.com/JohnYanez95/voice-scribe"
abstract: >-
  A local-first speech-to-text system for developer workflows. Runs
  faster-whisper on a local GPU and streams transcription over a
  WebSocket session in which text stabilizes incrementally: a partial
  tail resolves into committed text that is append-only and never
  revised, under a LocalAgreement-2 commit policy specified
  clause-by-clause and enforced by tests that cite the clause they
  check. No cloud services, no stored audio, no retained transcripts.
keywords:
  - speech-to-text
  - automatic-speech-recognition
  - streaming
  - whisper
  - local-first
  - privacy
  - voice-activity-detection
license: Apache-2.0
version: 4.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-07"

